/code-review high 2026-10-09-kotlin-language-stack

1. plugins/vwf/skills/init/SKILL.md:356 — The new Gradle rows have no root-only guard, unlike the .xcodeproj row. A Flutter app's android/settings.gradle(.kts) (and React Native's android/ folder) is now read as a separate kotlin project. Failure: init in source mode walks every directory below the root. For any Flutter app it finds android/settings.gradle.kts and proposes an extra kotlin sub-project. The Flutter pack says those Gradle files are subordinate to pubspec.yaml, and the .xcodeproj row is root-only for exactly this reason (ios/Runner.xcodeproj).
2. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/install/kotlin:20 — Plain ./gradlew dependencies (and --write-locks) only runs on the root project, so in a multi-module build no module's configurations are resolved or locked. Failure: the bundle describes a root settings.gradle.kts with modules under it. Gradle's locking docs say dependencies runs only on the root project, and the pack's own locking.md says to run it per module or use a resolveAndLockAll task. Install/upgrade never write or check core/gradle.lockfile, and under STRICT lock mode the module builds then fail on missing lock state.
3. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/install/kotlin:18 — The lockfile check relies on the dependencies report task, which resolves leniently: a lock-state mismatch shows as FAILED in the report but the task still exits 0. The documented claim that install "fails when the resolved graph disagrees with gradle.lockfile" does not hold. Failure: someone edits the catalog without re-locking. CI runs setup:deps:install --frozen, the report prints the mismatch, BUILD SUCCESSFUL is returned and the stale lock passes the gate. --frozen also only covers the case where no lockfile exists.
4. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/install/kotlin:18 — The branch keys on the root gradle.lockfile only. In a multi-module build whose root locks nothing, that file never exists, even though pack.yaml declares **/gradle.lockfile. Failure: the modules are locked but the root has no lockfile. Every non-frozen install takes the --write-locks path (install rewrites locks, which the pack forbids), and every --frozen CI run exits 1 with "no gradle.lockfile" although the modules are fully locked.
5. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/audit/kotlin:23 — The audit scans only the root gradle.lockfile (and skips entirely when it is missing). Module lockfiles (**/gradle.lockfile) and settings-gradle.lockfile, all declared in the gradle pack, are never audited. Failure: in a multi-module library the vulnerable dependency sits in core/gradle.lockfile. setup:deps:audit:kotlin either reports nothing to audit or scans an empty root lock. grype dir:. (or looping over the declared globs) would cover every lockfile.
6. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-gate/detekt/config/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/detekt:48 — detekt runs with --input . and excludes only build/.gradle/.kotlin/generated. It ignores .gitignore, while the Kotlin check uses git ls-files and the ktlint tasks lint only git-listed files. Failure: in a monorepo with a React Native or Capacitor frontend, node_modules/**/android/**/*.kt is linted, as are sibling git worktrees under .worktrees/ or .claude/worktrees/. With maxIssues: 0 and warningsAsErrors, code:lint:all fails on third-party code nobody owns.
7. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/config/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/install/kotlin:12 — When ./gradlew is missing, install exits 0 with a warning even under --frozen. The Swift equivalent exits 1 when its toolchain is missing. Failure: a Kotlin repo that forgot to commit the wrapper (or lost the exec bit) passes setup:deps:install --frozen in CI with nothing resolved.
8. plugins/stackgen/stacks/language/kotlin/conventions.md:66 — The doctrine on the gradle-versions-plugin contradicts itself. kotlin says the settings plugin io.github.ben-manes.versions.settings goes in settings.gradle.kts with its version in the catalog. The gradle pack's version-catalog.md says com.github.ben-manes.versions goes in [plugins], applied at the root build. Failure: the version catalog is not available inside the plugins {} block of settings.gradle.kts, so "its version in the catalog" cannot be written; the two packs teach incompatible setups for the one task setup:deps:outdated:kotlin depends on.
9. plugins/vwf/skills/init/SKILL.md:356 — Any Groovy settings.gradle or build.gradle maps to kotlin, so a plain Java/Gradle repo is labelled Kotlin. The language pack's own manifest fact is settings.gradle.kts alone. Failure: a Java-only Gradle project is proposed as a kotlin sub-project and steered toward the kotlin-library bundle.
10. plugins/stackgen/stacks/toolchain-gate/ktlint/config/.config/mise/tasks/code/format/ktlint:98 — Without --fix, code:format:ktlint runs exactly the same ktlint lint as code:lint:ktlint; ~90 lines of copy-paste differing only in the final call. Failure: a check-mode run of code:format:all plus code:lint:all starts ktlint twice over the same file list and reports every finding twice.
